  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{2}{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{2}{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{2}{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}]}_{a}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{3}^{x}]}_{a}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({3}^{2}-{3}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}\\cdot (9-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{3}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={3}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{3}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{3}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067475/assets/abae6131aceb7348a82ea01a544b28a62d8835b7857da14a6339b4ae3b88a1fd.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}\\cdot (9-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{3}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}\\cdot (9-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
